{"seq":11,"trial_id":"gbrain-scoped-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-told-scoped-mu-heldout/ho-04-hartford-summary/r4","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T12:33:47.509Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"4318fa30e6c561782fc525fbd590faa7a44d8f2013a73338f6dd64f5c7920032","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1X6KN92LKD","text":"@Gideon Sato, here's a draft for Mateo's procurement team. I haven't sent it anywhere. Please review it before forwarding.\n\n**Hartford gate kiosks outage (VTG), 3 Aug 2026: summary**\n\n- **First report:** 08:12, SUP-5380 (Sev 1). Kiosk check-in failed and drivers were queuing. The incident room #inc-vtg-hartford opened at 10:42 with both inbound lanes showing a white screen after badge scan.\n- **Kiosk 1 back:** 11:03. The first trailer was checked in (trailer 8836) and dispatch could see it.\n- **Both lanes confirmed working:** 11:07, per the incident room update at 11:08. The incident is left open for another arrival cycle.\n- **Still open:** Mateo's account cannot open the status page. Screenshot is attached to INC-4821. Scheduling and gate check-in via Pemberline Dock work.\n\nSource: #inc-vtg-hartford and SUP-5380. The 08:12 time is from the ticket's update log, so it's earlier than the incident room opening at 10:42. If procurement needs the 08:12 time explained, that's worth a line in the note."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1X6KN92LKD","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
